  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1: Nor'easter will bring gusty winds and periods of\nrain for the first weekend of Fall \n\nSensible weather conditions continue to trend incrementally \nbearish on the margin particularly later Saturday through \nSunday as wind and rain impacts extend westward from powerful \nNor'easter tracking toward the NJ/Long Island/southern New \nEngland coast. Latest model guidance favored a minor increase in\nwind gusts and westward expansion of higher POPs/QPF to the \nAllegheny Front. Locations throughout the Susquehanna Valley \nwill see the most persistent rain and strongest wind gusts up to\n40 mph. We lowered max temps a few degrees Sunday due to the \ncombination of clouds, wind, and rain. We can't rule out some \nlocalized/minor impacts (sporadic power outages and tree damage)\ndue to the wind gusts especially across the eastern portions of\nthe CWA. \n\nIt's still hard to say how far west the precip will reach with\nthe western Alleghenies most likely to continue an extended dry\nstretch through much of next week. As the nor'easter lifts to\nthe northeast, conditions should steadily improve by the middle\nof next week with temperatures poised to rebound above the\nhistorical average for the end of September.",
